+# Todo Due Dates Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Implement ticket #1: optional due dates, computed overdue status, API filtering, and the “nur überfällige” list control.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep data in the existing in-memory store. Store `dueDate` as a calendar-date string or `null` and compute `overdue` when returning a todo using the current UTC day; inject a clock into `createStore` for deterministic boundary tests. The page uses the API filter and renders text with DOM APIs.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24 builtins, node:test, plain HTML and JavaScript; Playwright MCP for browser verification.
+
+**Spec:** Approved conversation scope for Gitea ticket #1, “Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos”, including the user's API and UI filter additions.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` and map to HTTP 400.
+- TDD: write a failing test in `test/` first.
+- `dueDate` is optional on POST, defaults to `null`, and accepts only `null` or a real calendar date in `YYYY-MM-DD` format; PATCH can replace or remove it with `null`, and omission preserves it.
+- Every returned todo has `dueDate` and boolean `overdue`; overdue means unfinished with a date strictly before today in UTC. No date means never overdue.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` returns only overdue todos. Other requests retain the unfiltered list; preserve insertion order. No additional filter modes.
+- Show a todo's date when present, the exact word “überfällig” only when overdue, and an initially unchecked checkbox labeled “nur überfällige”. Toggling it fetches filtered/all todos through the API.
+- Existing and new elements relied on by browser tests carry `data-testid`: `todo-list`, `todo-item`, `todo-title`, `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`, `overdue-filter`.
+- The agent tests end to end in the running app, saves evidence outside the repository, and stops the app afterward.
+- No sorting, reminders, styling, dependencies, or other product features.
+- Finish on branch `1_faelligkeitsdatum_fuer_todos`; create a draft PR against `main`, never merge or close the ticket.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- UTC midnight: an existing todo must become overdue without being updated; Task 1 pins this with an injected clock, including a non-UTC offset.
+- Calendar validation: reject rollover dates, malformed formats, invalid types, and non-leap-year February 29; Task 1 also accepts leap-year February 29.
+- Rejected PATCH: invalid date or boolean must leave the entire todo unchanged; Task 1 tests a combined title/date/done patch.
+- Mixed datasets: filters must exclude completed, undated, today, and future todos while preserving order; Task 1 checks HTTP results and Task 2 checks the browser.
+- Repeated UI changes: switching the filter on, off, and on again must replace rows without duplicates, including an empty filtered result; Task 2 verifies this in Playwright.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Due dates and overdue API
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/store.mjs`, `src/app.mjs`, `test/app.test.mjs`; create `test/store.test.mjs`.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: existing `ValidationError`, `createApp(store = createStore())`, and store CRUD methods.
+- Produces: `createStore(now = () => new Date())`; returned todo snapshots `{ id, title, done, dueDate, overdue }`; `GET /todos?overdue=true` filters the computed boolean.
+
+- [x] **Step 1: Write failing store tests.** Assert default `dueDate: null` and `overdue: false`; setting, preserving, changing, and clearing due dates; yesterday/today/tomorrow, done, and undated status; moving a clock from `2026-10-15T23:59:59.999Z` to `2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z` changes status for a todo due October 15. A clock at `2026-10-15T23:30:00-02:00` must use October 16 UTC. Reject `2026-02-29`, `2026-04-31`, empty/whitespace strings, timestamps, non-padded dates, numbers, booleans, arrays, and objects; accept `2028-02-29`. Verify a rejected combined PATCH does not partially change title, done, or date.
+- [x] **Step 2: Verify red.** Run `node --test test/store.test.mjs`; confirm assertions fail because due-date and computed status support are missing.
+- [x] **Step 3: Implement store support.** Validate dates using an exact format and UTC calendar round-trip, validate the full PATCH before mutating, and return snapshots with freshly computed status. Keep persisted records free of derived status. Do not change unrelated request validation.
+- [x] **Step 4: Verify green.** Run `node --test test/store.test.mjs`; all store cases pass. Adjust the original full-object API assertion to include the agreed new fields.
+- [x] **Step 5: Write failing HTTP tests.** Use the real server and deterministic store clock. Check POST/PATCH/GET/list expose `dueDate` and `overdue`; invalid POST/PATCH dates return 400 with `error` and leave data unchanged; removing a date works; filtered GET returns only overdue ids from mixed data, unfiltered GET returns all in insertion order, and filtering an empty store yields `[]`.
+- [x] **Step 6: Verify red.** Run `npm test`; confirm the HTTP filter assertions fail because the route still returns all records.
+- [x] **Step 7: Implement the filter.** In the existing list route, filter `store.list()` by `todo.overdue` only when `url.searchParams.get('overdue') === 'true'`.
+- [x] **Step 8: Verify green and commit.** Run `npm test`; all tests pass. Commit store, API, and tests as `feat: add todo due dates and overdue API filter`.
+
+### Task 2: List control and end-to-end verification
+
+**Files:** Modify `public/index.html`, `test/app.test.mjs`.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: Task 1 todo fields and `GET /todos?overdue=true`.
+- Produces: visible due dates, “überfällig” text for overdue rows, and an accessible checkbox labeled “nur überfällige” that requests filtered/all rows.
+
+- [x] **Step 1: Write a failing page test.** Extend the served-page test to assert an accessible labeled checkbox with `data-testid="overdue-filter"`; do not test script source or implementation structure.
+- [x] **Step 2: Verify red.** Run `npm test`; the page test fails because the checkbox is absent.
+- [x] **Step 3: Implement the page.** Add the labeled checkbox and an async rendering function called initially and on change. Fetch `/todos?overdue=true` when checked and `/todos` when unchecked; replace list rows after each response. Use DOM text nodes and `textContent`; give dates and overdue labels the specified testids. Ensure rapid toggles cannot let an older response replace the latest selected state.
+- [x] **Step 4: Verify green.** Run `npm test`; all tests pass.
+- [x] **Step 5: Verify end to end with Playwright MCP.** Start `PORT=3000 npm start` and verify `/health`. Seed yesterday/today/tomorrow/undated/done records via the running API. In the browser assert all rows, dates, and overdue labels; click the checkbox, assert only overdue rows and the actual filtered request, uncheck and recheck without duplicate rows. Clear the remaining overdue date through PATCH, reload/toggle and assert an empty filtered list and recovery to all rows. Check invalid date HTTP 400. Save screenshots outside the repo and stop the app.
+- [x] **Step 6: Commit and review.** Commit as `feat: show due dates and filter overdue todos`. Use `superpowers:requesting-code-review` for a whole-branch review; fix relevant findings and rerun affected checks. Finish through `superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch`, applying agent-dev's mandatory draft PR and ticket summaries.
+
+## Execution results
+
+- Completed natively in the isolated branch worktree. Store and API tests were observed RED before implementation, then GREEN. Page control test was observed RED, then GREEN. Final suite: 34/34 passing.
+- Playwright MCP end-to-end checks passed for all planned scenarios, including delayed stale responses. Screenshots outside the repo: `/tmp/demo-todo-ticket-1-evidence/all-todos.png`, `only-overdue.png`, `no-overdue.png`. No browser console errors or warnings; app stopped afterward.
+- Independent whole-branch review: no Critical, Important, or Minor findings; 34/34 independently passing.
+- Review scope rulings:
+  - General malformed request-body validation remains outside this change — it is preexisting and explicitly excluded from Task 1 — existing malformed-body behavior can still occur.
+  - The browser fetches on load and filter changes without background midnight refresh — fresh status is computed on each API return and the user excluded additional features — an idle page can show its previous status until the next fetch.
+  - No new network-error display or retry controls — they are outside the approved minimal UI scope — failed fetches retain the existing minimal-page error behavior.
